title: A, but not B
mode: vhdl
chapter: Signals and gates
check: behaves
---- intro
Gates mix in one line. A light that is on when `a` is on **and `b` is off** is "a and (not b)":

| a | b | y |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | 0 | 0 |
| 0 | 1 | 0 |
| 1 | 0 | 1 |
| 1 | 1 | 0 |

`not` works on whatever comes right after it, so `a and not b` turns only `b` round.
---- task
Make `y` 1 only when `a` is 1 and `b` is 0.
---- start
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;

entity a_not_b is
  port(
    a : in  std_logic;
    b : in  std_logic;
    y : out std_logic
  );
end a_not_b;

architecture rtl of a_not_b is
begin
    -- write it here
end rtl;
---- answer
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;

entity a_not_b is
  port(
    a : in  std_logic;
    b : in  std_logic;
    y : out std_logic
  );
end a_not_b;

architecture rtl of a_not_b is
begin
    y <= a and not b;
end rtl;
---- hint1
An AND of `a` with the opposite of `b`.
---- hint2
`y <= a and not b;`
---- solution
`y <= a and not b;` The drawing shows a NOT gate on `b` going into an AND gate.
---- done
A machine that runs when start (`a`) is pressed but stops while a safety door (`b`) is open is this one line.
